<section class="ac-blue section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Stadium and venue retail questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does the POS work when stadium Wi-Fi goes down?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Store-and-Forward keeps every terminal selling through a network outage. Card data is encrypted at the point of capture and never stored on the POS; sales queue locally and sync to the back office when connectivity returns. During the halftime rush at a sold-out game, that keeps the line moving even when 50,000 fans saturate the network.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Does Teamwork Commerce handle food & beverage or merchandise?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce specializes in merchandise retail, team jerseys, hats, memorabilia, and fan gear. For F&B operations, Teamwork integrates with your existing concession POS or F&B vendor via open APIs. Unifying food and merchandise under one platform is the long-term goal, and Teamwork's open architecture is built to support that integration.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How quickly can seasonal staff learn the system?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The Colorado Rockies put new associates on registers in five minutes after they start. The iOS interface follows familiar design patterns that most people already know. For stadium retail where staff might work 20 games a year, this virtually eliminates training overhead.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does this compare to stadium-merchandise-only POS systems?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce covers the whole retail fleet, not just the stadium store. It is a broader platform than a merchandise-only system: native end-to-end RFID (not third-party), Store-and-Forward offline resilience (critical for network-saturated venues), integrated OMS with Endless Aisle and ship-from-store, real-time AI fan loyalty through the LAVA and Givex partnerships, and the full omnichannel stack (BOPIS, BORIS, cross-channel inventory). For venues that also operate standalone retail stores, like InnovaSport's 250 locations, Teamwork scales from the stadium to the entire retail fleet on one platform.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What fan spending data is available?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
